WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.005
A checklist for every tool you ship.

2
00:00:02.285 --> 00:00:07.128
Before a tool goes into the Studio 1 project, or anything else, run down this list.

3
00:00:07.408 --> 00:00:12.869
Does its description say what it does, when to use it, when not to, and what each parameter means?

4
00:00:13.149 --> 00:00:16.371
Is it read or write, and does its name make that obvious?

5
00:00:16.651 --> 00:00:20.619
If it writes, is it idempotent, is it reversible, and who approves it?

6
00:00:20.899 --> 00:00:23.053
Does it hold only the access it needs?

7
00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:27.173
Are inputs checked by a strict schema and by your own semantic checks?

8
00:00:27.453 --> 00:00:29.843
Do its errors tell the model what to do next?

9
00:00:30.123 --> 00:00:34.965
Does it return untrusted content, and if so, is that content marked as data?

10
00:00:35.245 --> 00:00:43.245
And is every call logged with its inputs, outcome, and error status, so that the evals you build in Studio 3 have something to measure?
